nd a bar chart comparing current staff with calculated need). Do not redesign, simplify, recolor, or rebrand the box. SET & PROPS: Small hospital meeting room in the afternoon: an oval table with a laptop connected to a projector, a screen showing a blurred budget table, two colleagues shown only as blurred shoulders, a pitcher of water and glasses, soft overhead light with blinds half closed. TIMELINE — 10 seconds: 0–2s Hook · close-up: projector screen with a blurred budget table (no readable text); cut to medium shot as she turns from the screen to the camera. VO (ID, verbatim): "Keuangan tanya, kenapa tambah pegawai?" Delivery (EN): calm, a bit tense 2–4s Problem · medium shot, she flips a printed page with only a short list. VO (ID, verbatim): "Usulan saya cuma daftar nama unit." Delivery (EN): honest 4–6s Problem · medium close-up, she glances at the blurred colleagues. VO (ID, verbatim): "Tanpa hitungan, susah meyakinkan." Delivery (EN): concerned 6–8s Problem · medium shot, she closes the laptop halfway. VO (ID, verbatim): "Usulannya ditunda lagi." Delivery (EN): quiet, disappointed 8–10s Beat · medium shot, she exhales and sets the page down. VO: none. AUDIO: Quiet meeting room ambience, projector fan hum, a pen tapping. Only the talent speaks. Natural Indonesian, conversational, clear pronunciation, no background music. Lighting/mood: realistic natural light matching the set, clean soft contrast, believable Indonesian setting, not glossy, not studio. Camera: follow the camera style above consistently; stable and restrained, no whip pans, no drone, no 360 orbit. Keep product readable whenever it is on screen. Performance: natural facial expression, believable professional UGC, natural eye contact, restrained gestures, no exaggerated acting. Lips clearly synced to each word. Hands: simple, natural, relaxed movements. CLEAN OUTPUT: No subtitles, captions, generated text overlays, watermark, poster layout, storyboard panels, or added graphics. Do not invent pr